{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.Figure8MuonMassCrossCheck","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.Figure8MuonMassCrossCheck","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MuonVolForm.muonRatioFromVol_eq_vol_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MuonVolForm.muonRatioFromVol_eq_vol_form","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/figure-8-muon-mass-cross-check.lean#L50-L61","doc":"Definitional form of the Vol-form muon ratio: `muonRatioFromVol q` is\n`Vol(4_1) / ℏ_q²` (the degenerate Borromean limit `λ_scale = 1`, `S = 0`).\n\nA definitional unfolding of `muonRatioFromVol`: the previous\n`muon_ratio_is_topological (q) (h_q_ne_one : q ≠ 1) : … := rfl` carried an\n**unused** `q ≠ 1` and a docstring claiming a reduction it did not derive.\nThe substantive CAL-2 content is `cal2_identity_pinned` above.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] figure-8 as Vol-form anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MuonVolForm.cal2_identity_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MuonVolForm.cal2_identity_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/figure-8-muon-mass-cross-check.lean#L36-L48","doc":"CAL-2 substrate identity (forward direction).\n\nThe CAL-2 calibration defines q₀ as the unique real solution of\n`m_μ/m_e = Vol(4_1)/ℏ_q²`.  Evaluating both sides at q₀\ntherefore gives equality by construction; the witness records\nthe 50-dps numerical match to 1.45 × 10⁻³⁰ ppm.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] CAL-2 in three-calibration-inputs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MuonVolForm.muonRatioFromVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MuonVolForm.muonRatioFromVol","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/figure-8-muon-mass-cross-check.lean#L27-L34","doc":"The muon-to-electron mass ratio in the Vol-form ansatz.\n\nWith λ_scale = 1 (no scaling) and S(4_1) = 0 (orientation\ntrivial), the topological-mass formula\n`m_μ / m_e = Vol(K)/ℏ_q² · λ + S` reduces to\n`m_μ / m_e = Vol(4_1) / ℏ_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MuonVolForm.hbarQSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MuonVolForm.hbarQSq","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/figure-8-muon-mass-cross-check.lean#L24-L25","doc":"ℏ_q² for convenience. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MuonVolForm.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MuonVolForm.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/figure-8-muon-mass-cross-check.lean#L21-L22","doc":"q-deformed Planck constant ℏ_q = (q − 1)/q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MuonVolForm.vol_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MuonVolForm.vol_4_1","kind":"def","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/figure-8-muon-mass-cross-check.lean#L17-L19","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the figure-8 knot complement\n`Vol(4_1) = 2 · Cl₂(π/3)` (Thurston / SnapPy). ","signatureChunk":0}]}